      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. For q-120295 and q-86616, a point on the positive x-axis has polar coordinates (r,0). For q-120981, the roots are a=arccos(9/11) and 2π−a, whose product rounds to 3.5. For q-20214, the roots are ±5π/6, giving −25π²/36. For q-141278, the sine difference formula gives −sin(x). For q-24650, the double-angle formula reduces the expression to 4. For q-120017, the expression equals 1, as does the stated choice (1/2)csc(π/6). For q-121264, arctan(15)≈86.1859° and the other root is 180° greater, giving 86° and 266°. Polar-to-Cartesian conversion uses (r cos θ,r sin θ), confirming q-120311, q-17137, and q-17134. For q-40826, A has angle 5π/4, so B has angle π/4 modulo 2π and radius 8. For q-120468, A has angle 7π/6, so B has angle 3π/2 and radius 4. For q-81224, B is antipodal to A, with angle 4π/3 and radius 10. For q-120597, the diagram places B in the fourth quadrant after the indicated counterclockwise rotation, giving angle 315° and coordinates (4,−4). For q-20849, dy/dx=(8t)/2=4t, which is zero at t=0. Each evidence string is a contiguous verbatim substring of that question's captured solution.",
